{% comment %}
  Featured & Latest Articles — controlled top feed for /pages/blog

  Implements Tim's decisions of 25–27 Aug 2026, including the three
  current-head corrections against head be22a706.

  CONTRACT
  - Eligibility: the exact tag "featured".
  - Order: ARTICLE integer metafield custom.featured_rank, ascending.
  - Positions 1..featured_slots are rank-ordered eligible articles.
  - Remaining positions fill with the newest published non-featured articles.
  - Hard maximum of nine cards, enforced in schema AND in code.
  - Drafts excluded: Liquid's blog.articles exposes published articles only.
  - No duplicate articles: the ledger keys on article.id, globally unique.

  BLOG DISCOVERY — WHY A HANDLE LIST IS UNAVOIDABLE
  Shopify Liquid cannot enumerate blogs. The blogs object is a lookup accessed
  by handle, not an iterable collection, so `for x in blogs` yields nothing and
  the candidate pool comes back empty. The blogs to scan therefore have to be
  named in a setting, which is the same mechanism already in use and already
  accepted on the hub search section.

  This is a blog handle list, not an article list. No article handle, ID or
  title appears anywhere in this file. Which articles are featured, and in what
  order, remains driven entirely by the live tag and the live rank metafield.
  A configured handle that resolves to no blog raises the HOLD reason
  unknown_blog_handle rather than being skipped, so a blog cannot silently drop
  out of validation.

  NO HARD-CODED ARTICLES
  No article handle, ID or title, and no blog handle list. Blogs are discovered
  by iterating the blogs global. Eligibility comes from live tag data, order
  from a live metafield. The only literals are slot counts, which are settings.

  WHY `article.tags contains 'featured'` IS THE EXACT TEST
  In Liquid, `contains` on an ARRAY tests for an exact element match, so this
  matches only the literal tag "featured" and never "featured:top" or any other
  legacy featured:* value. Do not pipe article.tags through a join filter first;
  joining makes it a string and turns the test into a substring match.

  CORRECTION 1 — COMPLETE TRAVERSAL, PROVEN NOT ASSUMED
  blog.articles has a default fetch page size of 50 per blog, and a for loop's
  limit parameter cannot raise it. The previous head passed an inflated limit
  value, which was ineffective. Every loop here is therefore scoped to a blog
  than to a combined 84-article array, so each traversal stays inside the
  documented bound.

  Rather than assume that is sufficient, this section verifies it. During
  validation it counts every article actually scanned and compares that to the
  sum of blog.articles_count across all blogs. If the platform ever truncates a
  fetch, scanned will fall short of expected and the feed raises the HOLD reason
  incomplete_traversal instead of publishing a false PASS. Both numbers are
  printed in the view-source readback, so completeness is provable rather than
  asserted.

  Rendering avoids re-traversal entirely. Validation records blog_handle/
  article_handle per rank, and rendering resolves each rank through the
  articles global. The only remaining multi-blog loop is the newest-fill pass,
  which is explicitly capped at 50 and always terminates far earlier because at
  most featured_slots articles are excluded from a 9-card grid.

  CORRECTION 2 — QA PANEL VISIBILITY
  The Liquid request object exposes no query-string-bearing url property, so the
  previous server-side query-string test was dead code. The HOLD panel
  is now NOT rendered into the shopper DOM at all. It is constructed client-side
  from the grid's data attributes only when window.location.search carries
  feed_qa=1. In the theme editor it is rendered server-side via request.design_mode.
  A shopper on the normal URL receives no panel markup whatsoever.

  CORRECTION 3 — HARD NINE-CARD CAP
  The schema range now stops at 9, and the value is additionally clamped in code
  so a settings file edited outside the theme editor cannot exceed the approved
  maximum.

  HOLD BEHAVIOUR
  A missing, duplicate, non-integer or out-of-range rank is a HOLD and must not
  silently fall back to newest-first for an approved article. The rank-pinning
  pass is gated on a valid state, so on HOLD it does not execute at all and no
  approved article can appear in an unapproved position.

  KNOWN LIMIT, documented and deliberately not worked around:
  a single blog holding more than 50 published articles would exceed the per-blog
  fetch page size. Largest blog today is 25. The incomplete_traversal check above
  would detect and HOLD on that condition rather than fail silently.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'component-article-card.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'section-main-blog.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }

  .featured-feed-hold {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    border: 2px solid #b00020;
    background: #fff5f5;
    color: #b00020;
    padding: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .featured-feed-hold h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 15px; }
  .featured-feed-hold ul { margin: 8px 0 0 18px; }
  .featured-feed-hold code { background: #ffe9e9; padding: 1px 4px; }
{%- endstyle -%}

{%- liquid
  assign featured_slots = section.settings.featured_slots | default: 6

    # Correction 3: clamp in code as well as in the schema.
  assign max_cards = section.settings.max_cards | default: 9
  if max_cards > 9
    assign max_cards = 9
  endif
  if max_cards < 1
    assign max_cards = 1
  endif

    # Validation pass. Scoped per blog so every loop stays inside the documented
    # per-array fetch bound, with scanned-vs-expected proof of completeness.
  assign expected_total = 0
  assign scanned_total = 0
  assign eligible_count = 0
  assign seen_ranks = '|'
  assign hold_reasons = '|'
  assign rank_map = '|'
  assign rank_readback = ''

  assign blog_handles = section.settings.blog_handles | split: ','
  assign blog_count = 0

  for handle in blog_handles
    assign clean_handle = handle | strip
    assign store_blog = blogs[clean_handle]

    if store_blog == blank
        # A configured handle that resolves to no blog is a HOLD. Silently
        # skipping it would hide an entire blog from validation.
      unless hold_reasons contains '|unknown_blog_handle|'
        assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: 'unknown_blog_handle|'
      endunless
      continue
    endif

    assign blog_count = blog_count | plus: 1
    assign expected_total = expected_total | plus: store_blog.articles_count

    for article in store_blog.articles
      assign scanned_total = scanned_total | plus: 1

      if article.tags contains 'featured'
        assign eligible_count = eligible_count | plus: 1
        assign rank_field = article.metafields.custom.featured_rank
        assign row_state = 'ok'

        if rank_field == blank
          assign row_state = 'missing_rank'
        else
          assign rank_num = rank_field.value | plus: 0
          assign rank_int = rank_num | round

          if rank_num != rank_int
            assign row_state = 'non_integer_rank'
          elsif rank_num < 1 or rank_num > featured_slots
            assign row_state = 'out_of_range_rank'
          else
            assign rank_key = '|' | append: rank_int | append: '|'
            if seen_ranks contains rank_key
              assign row_state = 'duplicate_rank'
            else
              assign lookup = store_blog.handle | append: '/' | append: article.handle
                # Resolve the lookup now, during validation. If it fails at
                # render time instead, the article would vanish from the
                # approved order with no reason code, which is the silent
                # fallback this section exists to prevent.
              if articles[lookup] == blank
                assign row_state = 'rank_lookup_failed'
              else
                assign seen_ranks = seen_ranks | append: rank_int | append: '|'
                assign rank_map = rank_map | append: rank_int | append: '>' | append: lookup | append: '|'
              endif
            endif
          endif
        endif

        unless row_state == 'ok'
          assign reason_key = '|' | append: row_state | append: '|'
          unless hold_reasons contains reason_key
            assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: row_state | append: '|'
          endunless
        endunless

        assign rank_display = rank_field.value | default: 'none'
        assign rank_readback = rank_readback | append: store_blog.handle | append: '/' | append: article.handle | append: ' rank=' | append: rank_display | append: ' state=' | append: row_state | append: '~'
      endif
    endfor
  endfor

    # Completeness check. A short scan means the platform truncated a fetch, so
    # the PASS/HOLD verdict cannot be trusted and the feed HOLDs.
    # An empty pool means blog resolution failed outright. Without this an
    # expected total of zero would equal a scanned total of zero and the
    # completeness check would pass while nothing had been examined at all.
  if expected_total == 0
    unless hold_reasons contains '|no_articles_found|'
      assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: 'no_articles_found|'
    endunless
  endif

  if scanned_total != expected_total
    unless hold_reasons contains '|incomplete_traversal|'
      assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: 'incomplete_traversal|'
    endunless
  endif

    # Fewer eligible articles than ranked slots means the tag has not been fully
    # applied yet.
  if eligible_count < featured_slots
    unless hold_reasons contains '|incomplete_eligible_set|'
      assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: 'incomplete_eligible_set|'
    endunless
  endif

    # Fill window. The fill pass skips every eligible article before it can
    # place a card, so the window must cover them plus the whole grid. Clamped
    # to the documented per-array bound; if that clamp binds, HOLD rather than
    # silently render a short grid.
  assign fill_limit = max_cards | plus: eligible_count
  if fill_limit > 50
    assign fill_limit = 50
    unless hold_reasons contains '|fill_window_exhausted|'
      assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: 'fill_window_exhausted|'
    endunless
  endif

  assign feed_state = 'ok'
  if hold_reasons != '|'
    assign feed_state = 'hold'
  endif

  assign reason_list = hold_reasons | remove_first: '|' | split: '|'
  assign rank_entries = rank_map | remove_first: '|' | split: '|'

    # Newest-first pool, used only by the fill pass.
  assign pool = '' | split: ''
  for handle in blog_handles
    assign clean_handle = handle | strip
    assign store_blog = blogs[clean_handle]
    if store_blog != blank
      assign pool = pool | concat: store_blog.articles
    endif
  endfor
  assign pool_newest = pool | sort: 'published_at' | reverse

  assign rendered = '|'
  assign card_count = 0
-%}

{%- comment -%} View-source readback. Present on every render, so state is provable. {%- endcomment -%}
<!-- FEATURED_FEED_READBACK
  state: {{ feed_state }}
  traversal: scanned {{ scanned_total }} of {{ expected_total }} expected articles across {{ blog_count }} resolved blogs
  eligible (exact tag "featured"): {{ eligible_count }} of {{ featured_slots }} ranked slots
  max cards (clamped): {{ max_cards }} | fill window: {{ fill_limit }}
  hold reasons: {% if reason_list.size > 0 %}{{ reason_list | join: ', ' }}{% else %}none{% endif %}
  eligible readback:
{% if rank_readback != blank %}{% assign readback_lines = rank_readback | split: '~' %}{% for readback_line in readback_lines %}    {{ readback_line }}
{% endfor %}{% else %}    (no eligible articles)
{% endif %}-->

<div class="main-blog page-width section-{{ section.id }}-padding">
  {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
    <h2 class="title--primary">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if section.settings.description != blank -%}
    <div class="main-blog-description">{{ section.settings.description }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div
    class="blog-articles blog-articles--featured-latest"
    data-featured-feed
    data-feed-state="{{ feed_state }}"
    data-scanned-total="{{ scanned_total }}"
    data-expected-total="{{ expected_total }}"
    data-eligible-count="{{ eligible_count }}"
    data-featured-slots="{{ featured_slots }}"
    data-max-cards="{{ max_cards }}"
    data-hold-reasons="{% if reason_list.size > 0 %}{{ reason_list | join: ',' }}{% endif %}"
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      Correction 2: the panel is rendered server-side ONLY in the theme editor.
      On the storefront it is absent from the DOM and is built client-side only
      when feed_qa=1 is present, so shoppers never receive the markup.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if feed_state == 'hold' and request.design_mode -%}
      <div class="featured-feed-hold">
        <h3>Featured feed is on HOLD — rank data is not valid</h3>
        <p>
          No approved article has been pinned. Positions are filled with newest
          published articles only, so no approved article appears in an
          unapproved position.
        </p>
        <ul>
          {%- for reason in reason_list -%}
            <li>{{ reason | replace: '_', ' ' }}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
        <p>
          Traversal: scanned {{ scanned_total }} of {{ expected_total }} expected articles.
          Eligible: {{ eligible_count }} of {{ featured_slots }}.
        </p>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Pass 1 — rank-ordered featured articles. Runs only when every rank is
      valid. Ranks resolve through the articles global, so no re-traversal.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if feed_state == 'ok' -%}
      {%- for position in (1..featured_slots) -%}
        {%- if card_count >= max_cards -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- for entry in rank_entries -%}
          {%- assign parts = entry | split: '>' -%}
          {%- assign entry_rank = parts[0] | plus: 0 -%}
          {%- if entry_rank == position -%}
            {%- assign ranked_article = articles[parts[1]] -%}
            {%- if ranked_article != blank -%}
              {%- assign key = '|' | append: ranked_article.id | append: '|' -%}
              {%- unless rendered contains key -%}
                {% render 'article-card',
                  article: ranked_article,
                  media_height: section.settings.image_height,
                  media_aspect_ratio: ranked_article.image.aspect_ratio,
                  show_image: section.settings.show_image,
                  show_date: section.settings.show_date,
                  show_author: section.settings.show_author,
                  show_excerpt: true
                %}
                {%- liquid
                  assign rendered = rendered | append: ranked_article.id | append: '|'
                  assign card_count = card_count | plus: 1
                -%}
              {%- endunless -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- break -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Pass 2 — fill remaining positions with newest non-featured articles.
      The window is sized to eligible_count plus max_cards, so every eligible
      article can be skipped and the grid still fills. Sizing is computed, not
      assumed, and raises fill_window_exhausted if it cannot be satisfied.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for article in pool_newest limit: fill_limit -%}
      {%- if card_count >= max_cards -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- unless article.tags contains 'featured' -%}
        {%- assign key = '|' | append: article.id | append: '|' -%}
        {%- unless rendered contains key -%}
          {% render 'article-card',
            article: article,
            media_height: section.settings.image_height,
            media_aspect_ratio: article.image.aspect_ratio,
            show_image: section.settings.show_image,
            show_date: section.settings.show_date,
            show_author: section.settings.show_author,
            show_excerpt: true
          %}
          {%- liquid
            assign rendered = rendered | append: article.id | append: '|'
            assign card_count = card_count | plus: 1
          -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  // Correction 2: QA panel is built client-side only on ?feed_qa=1.
  // Shoppers on the normal URL receive no panel markup at all.
  (function () {
    var params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    if (params.get('feed_qa') !== '1') return;

    var grid = document.querySelector('[data-featured-feed]');
    if (!grid || grid.dataset.feedState !== 'hold') return;
    if (grid.querySelector('.featured-feed-hold')) return; // already server-rendered in the editor

    var reasons = (grid.dataset.holdReasons || '').split(',').filter(Boolean);

    var panel = document.createElement('div');
    panel.className = 'featured-feed-hold';

    var title = document.createElement('h3');
    title.textContent = 'Featured feed is on HOLD \u2014 rank data is not valid';
    panel.appendChild(title);

    var intro = document.createElement('p');
    intro.textContent =
      'No approved article has been pinned. Positions are filled with newest ' +
      'published articles only, so no approved article appears in an unapproved position.';
    panel.appendChild(intro);

    if (reasons.length) {
      var list = document.createElement('ul');
      reasons.forEach(function (reason) {
        var li = document.createElement('li');
        li.textContent = reason.replace(/_/g, ' ');
        list.appendChild(li);
      });
      panel.appendChild(list);
    }

    var stats = document.createElement('p');
    stats.textContent =
      'Traversal: scanned ' + grid.dataset.scannedTotal + ' of ' +
      grid.dataset.expectedTotal + ' expected articles. Eligible: ' +
      grid.dataset.eligibleCount + ' of ' + grid.dataset.featuredSlots + '.';
    panel.appendChild(stats);

    grid.insertBefore(panel, grid.firstChild);
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Featured & Latest",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Featured & Latest Articles"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Section description"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Eligibility is the exact tag 'featured'. Order is the article metafield custom.featured_rank, ascending. Legacy tags such as 'featured:top' are ignored. Remaining positions fill with the newest published articles. Append ?feed_qa=1 to the page URL to reveal the HOLD diagnostic panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "blog_handles",
      "label": "Blog handles (comma separated)",
      "default": "buying-guides, comparisons, maintenance, warranty-shipping, news, case-studies",
      "info": "Liquid cannot enumerate blogs, so the blogs to scan must be named here. Article selection remains driven entirely by tag and rank. A handle that resolves to no blog is a HOLD."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "featured_slots",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 9,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Ranked featured positions",
      "default": 6,
      "info": "Valid featured_rank values are 1 to this number. Anything outside it is a HOLD."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_cards",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 9,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Maximum cards",
      "default": 9,
      "info": "Approved maximum is nine. The value is also clamped to nine in code."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_image", "default": true, "label": "Show image" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_date", "default": true, "label": "Show date" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_author", "default": false, "label": "Show author" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_height",
      "options": [
        { "value": "adapt", "label": "Adapt" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "medium",
      "label": "Image height"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "default": 36
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Featured & Latest" }]
}
{% endschema %}
